The Global Assessment Report on Disaster Risk Reduction (GAR) is UNDRR’s flagship global report on disaster risk, widely referenced by policymakers, donors, and practitioners.

The GAR landing needed to work for multiple audiences: policymakers, journalists, donors, and the general public. We framed the page around outcomes and choices rather than internal structure—short value‑dense sections, scannable claims tied to the report, and interactive elements that rewarded curiosity.

My role in the work bridged content, UX, and platform leadership: aligning editorial priorities with component patterns, setting performance budgets, and ensuring the page remained fast and accessible even as rich media was added.

## Problem

Flagship report launches often default to long pages with heavy media and abstract framing. We needed a landing that made the stakes clear in seconds, encouraged exploration, and stayed fast worldwide.

## Approach

- Outcomes‑first copy and headings; short sections that ladder to the report narrative.
- Interactive data visuals and embedded media balanced with accessibility.
- Performance guardrails (image pipelines, lazy loading, budget checks) to maintain CWV.

## Key decisions

- Prioritized a lead statement that connects macroeconomic stakes to personal and policy choices.
- Structured the page for quick scanning with clear onward paths to solutions and evidence.
- Tuned media loading and fallback content to keep the experience smooth.

## Outcomes

- Contributed to ~40% engagement lift during campaign period (vs prior comparable launch).
- Maintained fast, accessible experience with rich content.

